<title>TAIWAN: Macronix cuts '97 profit forecast.</title>
<headline>Macronix cuts '97 profit forecast.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macronix International Corp, one of Taiwan's leading semiconductor makers, said on Tuesday it was lowering its 1997 pretax profit forecast by 50 percent to T$1.3 billion from an earlier forecast of T$2.6 billion because of fierce competition.</p>
<p>&quot;The company's original financial forecasts are no longer applicable due to fierce competition and price fluctuations in the first half of this year,&quot; Macronix said in a statement.</p>
<p>After the revision, Macronix's per-share-earning was seen at T$2.12, it said.</p>
